  "expected_demo_result": "failed",
  "notes": "Deliberately ZERO-MARGIN twin of v1: identical planner, margin cut from 65 cm to 53 cm -- the exact minimum that still clears the geometry with nothing to spare. It is GREEN on all 16 scenarios at the 'nominal' domain and GREEN under 'actuation_degraded', then goes RED under 'obs_noise' on both keep_out rows (visible 3 and held-out 1): the perception error contributes -2.94 cm to the planned offset and the admissible margin floor rises from 53 to 56 cm, so the base clips the inflated restricted band and zone_clear fails (measured min_clearance_to_obstacle_cm 25.07 where v1 measures 37.07). That is the honest point of the domain sweep -- a policy that only just clears the geometry has no business shipping, and this file is the proof that the sweep can tell the difference."
}
